## Authentication

All authentication is handled via `Authenticator` implementations passed to the client constructor.

### Bearer Token

```kotlin statements
import {{invokerPackage}}.{{clientClassName}}
import {{invokerPackage}}.auth.BearerAuthenticator

val authenticator = BearerAuthenticator("https://api.example.com", "your-token")
val client = {{clientClassName}}(authenticator)
```

A credential you pass wins; when you pass none, the authenticator reads `{{envVarPrefix}}_TOKEN` (Basic auth: `{{envVarPrefix}}_USERNAME` and `{{envVarPrefix}}_PASSWORD`, API key: `{{envVarPrefix}}_API_KEY`) once, when it is built, and an empty value counts as unset. A missing credential fails right there with an `IllegalArgumentException` naming the variable. A token that rotates takes `BearerAuthenticator(host, tokenProvider = { currentToken() })`, called on every request (`ApiKeyAuthenticator` has `apiKeyProvider`); a provider is used only when no argument and no environment variable is set.

{{#hasSecuritySchemeEnvVars}}
The authenticator generated for a security scheme reads its own variable instead:

{{#securitySchemeEnvVars}}
- `{{envName}}`: the `{{field}}` of the `{{schemeId}}` scheme
{{/securitySchemeEnvVars}}

{{/hasSecuritySchemeEnvVars}}
{{#hasClientSchemes}}
### Credentials per security scheme

`{{clientClassName}}(host, <scheme> = credential, transportOptions)` takes one optional credential for each security scheme of the API, named after the scheme:{{#clientSchemes}} `{{{argName}}}`{{^-last}},{{/-last}}{{/clientSchemes}}. Each operation uses the credential of the first scheme its spec lists that you passed; a call cannot pick another scheme, so an options object has no authenticator. An operation none of whose schemes you passed a credential for uses the authenticator of `{{clientClassName}}(authenticator)` if you gave one and is otherwise sent without a credential, and an operation declared with no security never sends one.

```kotlin statements
{{#clientSchemes}}
{{#-first}}
import {{invokerPackage}}.{{clientClassName}}
import {{authPackage}}.{{className}}

/* The credential of the scheme comes from the environment. */
val client = {{clientClassName}}("https://api.example.com", {{{argName}}} = {{className}}("https://api.example.com"))
{{/-first}}
{{/clientSchemes}}
```

{{/hasClientSchemes}}
